cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kvorum in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "kvorum: a strongly consistent key-value store on a from-scratch Raft"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: sadrax4
repository-code: "https://github.com/sadrax4/kvorum"
url: "https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/sadrax4/kvorum"
abstract: >-
  kvorum is a distributed, strongly consistent key-value store written in Go.
  Its consensus core is a from-scratch, deterministic implementation of the
  Raft algorithm, verified by a seeded simulation harness that injects network
  partitions, message loss, reordering, and crashes.
keywords:
  - raft
  - consensus
  - distributed-systems
  - key-value-store
  - go
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
